ML-UMA pair style and uma-engine
================================

The C++ pair style (`pair_uma.cpp`, `pair_uma.h`) and the uma-engine library
are contributed to LAMMPS and are distributed under the GNU General Public
License version 2, the same license as LAMMPS itself.

  Contributing author: Xiaoli Yan, Argonne National Laboratory (xyan11@anl.gov)

This package **does not redistribute** FairChem UMA model weights. At run time
LAMMPS loads a user-supplied TorchScript artifact directory (`pair_coeff`).
Export scripts may read a user-supplied FairChem checkpoint file
(`UMA_CHECKPOINT`). Those files remain under Meta / FairChem's own terms.

Third-party code vendored here
------------------------------

* `uma-engine/third_party/vesin/` — BSD-3-Clause (Guillaume Fraux). See
  `uma-engine/third_party/vesin/LICENSE`.
* `uma-engine/third_party/nlohmann/json.hpp` — MIT (nlohmann).
* `uma-engine/third_party/nccl/include/nccl.h` — NVIDIA NCCL header. Use is
  subject to the NCCL license shipped with the CUDA toolkit; prefer the
  toolkit header when building with CUDA.

Dependencies not shipped
------------------------

* LibTorch / PyTorch — BSD-style license (separate install).
* fairchem-core (export / optional Python GP worker only) — MIT.
* FairChem UMA checkpoints (`facebook/UMA` on Hugging Face, e.g. uma-s-1p2.pt)
  — gated **FAIR Chemistry License** (commercially permissive, separate from
  FairChem's MIT software license; geographic / acceptable-use restrictions).
  Not part of this source tree. Users must accept those terms themselves.
